<title>SWEDEN: Atlas Copco 9 mo profit up 9 pct.</title>
<headline>Atlas Copco 9 mo profit up 9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial engineering group Atlas Copco report for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		2,232   vs   2,054</p>
<p> Sales				    18,317   vs  17,771</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)	     7.74   vs     7.30</p>
<p> Operating expenses		     15,623 vs  15,341</p>
<p> Depreciation				  571 vs     517</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	 2,123 vs   1,913</p>
<p> Interest net				  102 vs     104</p>
<p> Dividends received			   11 vs	 1</p>
<p> Finance exchange differences    CHARGE  4 vs	28 CHARGE</p>
<p> Associate interests			   0 vs	64</p>
<p> Tax					    793  vs     693</p>
<p> Minorities			CHARGE    19  vs	22 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,420  vs   1,339</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Atlas Copco AB</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 13 analyst found an average expectation of a profit after financial items of 2.22 billion crowns for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
